{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And he said to his people.</b> He himself initiated the plan first. We say in the first chapter of Sotah: three were in that counsel, and Balaam is listed among them. And if you ask: how could he live so long, from before our birth until the war against Midian in the fortieth year after their going out from the land of Egypt — for we say in Chelek: it is written in Balaam's ledger that Balaam was thirty-three years old when Phinehas killed him as a bandit — one may answer: there were two Balaams, and this one was the father of his father. And his grandson was called Balaam after his grandfather. And some say: three were in that counsel for harlotry with the daughters of Moab."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Reading המ׳‎ as המ׳ = הארבעים (forty), and resolving פ״‎ק as פרק קדמא (first chapter) and י״‎מ as יש אומרים by convention."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:43.719444269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}